# bower — front-end package manager (legacy)

Bower is deprecated — new projects should use npm/yarn. Kept for maintaining older front-end projects.

## Install packages locally

```sh
bower install <package-name>

# Directly from github
bower install <user>/<repo>

# Specific version
bower install <package-name>#<version>

# Install and save to bower.json
bower install <package-name> --save
```

## Inspect

```sh
bower info <package-name>
bower list
bower search <package-name>
```

## Update / remove

```sh
bower update <package-name>
bower uninstall <package-name>
```

## Real-world: resurrect an old project on a fresh Tumbleweed box

```sh
sudo npm install -g bower
cd ~/Public/old-webapp
bower install          # reads bower.json, restores bower_components/
```

| Flag       | What it does                     |
| ---------- | -------------------------------- |
| --save     | record in bower.json deps        |
| --save-dev | record in devDependencies        |
| -F         | force latest on conflicts        |
